{"id":4223385160,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/openmc_benchmark_plugin.py","line":null,"commit_id":"1cbc21b1cc46a1b5a7c8aeaf5217d09d04dec815","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:40:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:46:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223385160","body":"This monkeypatches `model_benchmark_zoo` internals (`BaseCommonGeometryObject.dagmc_model`, `export_stp_file`). If upstream renames or changes either one, the whole benchmark job fails at `pytest_configure`. Could we fix the deprecated `.save()` call and the ID handling in [model_benchmark_zoo](https://github.com/fusion-energy/model_benchmark_zoo) itself and drop this patch, or at least link an upstream issue here?"},
{"id":4223388435,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/openmc_benchmark_plugin.py","line":null,"commit_id":"a1e10ae03d55be8a16c80d00a4a9878051e1dfb1","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:41:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:41:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223388435","body":"Nit: the docstring opens with four quotes, so the text starts with a stray `\"`.\n\n```suggestion\n\"\"\"Reset OpenMC IDs between CSG and DAGMC models in benchmark comparisons.\"\"\"\n```"},
{"id":4223401410,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/test_assembly_with_materials.py","line":null,"commit_id":"cb0edbc50c2e214a33f99f5955e58c81f60d49a7","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:42:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:42:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223401410","body":"Renaming to `_tmpdir` silences Ruff, but the temp dir still isn't used and the h5m files are still written to the current directory. Either write the outputs into `tmpdir` (or use pytest's `tmp_path`), or remove the context manager. Same pattern in `tests/test_assembly_with_names.py` (lines 22, 58, 97)."},
{"id":4223409109,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/test_h5m_in_transport.py","line":null,"commit_id":"2a727c8c9e21f94de02c368166adb9b63fe4f1cd","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:43:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:43:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223409109","body":"Could we revert the mesh size change here? The comment isn't accurate (Gmsh's `Mesh.MeshSizeMin` defaults to 0), and moving from `{1: 0.9, 2: 0.1, 3: 0.9}` to sizes close to the default means a regression where per-volume `set_size` is ignored would still pass. Dropping `set_size` for backends other than gmsh also removes coverage of that path. Keeping the shared `set_size` variable is a nice tidy-up though.\n\n```suggestion\n    set_size = {1: 0.9, 2: 0.1, 3: 0.9}\n    h5m_file = model.export_dagmc_h5m_file(\n        filename=\"dagmc.h5m\",\n        set_size=set_size,\n        meshing_backend=meshing_backend,\n    )\n```"},
{"id":4223409326,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/test_python_api.py","line":null,"commit_id":"b58d11130c5e8f15caaf571827ccbf43f1c45bcd","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:43:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:43:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223409326","body":"Could we revert the mesh size change here? The comment isn't accurate (Gmsh's `Mesh.MeshSizeMin` defaults to 0), and moving from `{1: 0.9, 2: 0.1, 3: 0.9}` to sizes close to the default means a regression where per-volume `set_size` is ignored would still pass. Dropping `set_size` for backends other than gmsh also removes coverage of that path. Keeping the shared `set_size` variable is a nice tidy-up though.\n\n```suggestion\n    set_size = {1: 0.9, 2: 0.1, 3: 0.9}\n    h5m_file = tmp_path / \"dagmc.h5m\"\n    filename = model.export_dagmc_h5m_file(\n        filename=str(h5m_file),\n        set_size=set_size,\n        meshing_backend=meshing_backend,\n    )\n```"},
{"id":4223457940,"pr":228,"user":"shimwell","path":"tests/test_share_coincident_face_ids.py","line":57,"commit_id":"4b2be750355d1f17d2cd98eb6b2228913ac6fd81","in_reply_to_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T19:49:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T19:49:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/fusion-energy/cad_to_dagmc/pull/228#discussion_r4223457940","body":"Nit: setting `category = None` and then immediately checking for `None` is redundant. A `continue` inside the `except` does the same thing.\n\n```suggestion\n        except RuntimeError as exc:\n            if \"MOAB ErrorCode: MB_TAG_NOT_FOUND\" not in str(exc):\n                raise\n            continue\n```"},
